  "version": "0.10.19",
  "description": "Adds Shen and reworks official champions 002-007 and 009 as Lucian, Orianna, Briar, Sivir, Kled, Xayah and Yone. Version 0.10.19 targets Teamfight Manager 2 base 0.5.1 and uses the matching official 0.5.1 SDK. Yone remains on the dual-sword V7 route: idle and run retain both weapons, steel and Azakana basic attacks select separate body animations and caster-follow slashes, Q1/Q2 use skill_q12, Q3 uses skill_q3, W uses the Azakana-led skill_w_azakana action, and R keeps a dual-sword sequence. Version 0.10.19 hardens the pixel contract around strict hash-locked contact-sheet grids (motion 5x4, attack/Q 6x4, W 3x2 and R 5x3), an exclusive semantic weapon palette whose steel_dark/mid/highlight and azakana_dark/red/highlight colors cannot be satisfied by mask, belt, clothing or hair pixels, and per-frame hand-anchor-to-blade-tip geometry gates for continuity, minimum reach, distinct directions and tip clearance. Version 0.10.18 is retained only as failed history: it connected the animation tags and atlas extension but its shared generic color cues could falsely pass frames with a missing, merged or shortened sword, so it did not complete the dual-sword pixel contract. Damage, hit detection, cooldowns, Q stack progression, audio timing and the current W cone settlement are unchanged. The actor atlas remains 4262x88 with 18 tags while preserving the official 3502x88, 13-tag, 54-frame Dual Blader contract as an immutable prefix; only the Azakana attack and Q3 require 13 appended physical frames, for 67 packed body frames total. The BP central grid, post-pick assignment page, management card, compact portrait and scoreboard remain on the separate source-direct UI V6 route retained from 0.10.17: the shared 95x88 NinePatch still samples the top 88 rows of dual_blader_grid, central geometry stays unchanged, and assignment or edge cards retain the -9 logical baseline correction. A fresh 0.10.19 save is required to verify the V7 animation tree because older saves embed their previous behavior tree and do not migrate its CasterAnimation tags. A save first created on 0.10.5 or later can still validate the current W mechanics, but cannot prove that the V7 attack, Q3 or W body routes are active. Spirit Cleave remains a stateless 80-degree, 42000-range GameCtx cone scan with no process-global ledger, deals 35 + 45% Attack + 6% target maximum-health physical damage, and settles one shield tier for zero through five champions hit; Mod API 0.8 still requires the documented fixed 0.5-second cast and 8-second cooldown. Retired E and 0.10.4 rectangular-W native names remain no-op saved-data compatibility only so old embedded trees do not crash after BP. The broader legacy MatchUIRunner, ClientDatabase, picked-side splash, dragon, server and other-champion rewrites remain explicitly opt-in. Automated source, geometry and build checks do not constitute live visual acceptance; 0.10.19 remains pending fresh-save in-game verification.",
  "last_updated": "2026-07-22",
